  "reasoning": "This commit (\"migrating to SConcept in typesystem rules (isApplicable): runtime\") replaced the RuleSet.getParents() implementation, which previously returned only direct parent concept names via ConceptRegistry's getParentsNames(), with a call to SConceptOperations.getAllSuperConcepts(nextConcept, false) — returning the entire transitive supertype hierarchy instead of just direct parents. Since getParents() is meant to walk the hierarchy one level at a time (as used by the SingleTermRules BFS/traversal logic), using getAllSuperConcepts instead of getDirectSuperConcepts caused incorrect/duplicate rule lookups, leading to the typesystem error described in the bug (e.g., a+='d' failing). The fix simply swaps getAllSuperConcepts for getDirectSuperConcepts, directly reverting the semantic error introduced by this commit.",
